config MICROTRUST_TEEI
	tristate "Microtrust SOTER (iSee) TEE client driver"
	depends on OF
	depends on DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
	help
	  Driver for the normal-world side of Microtrust's SOTER (iSee) secure
	  OS, as used on MediaTek SoCs. It brings up the shared queues between
	  the two worlds, keeps a pool of memory the secure world can read, and
	  exposes the TEE client, the trusted-application file service and the
	  fingerprint client to user space (/dev/teei_client, /dev/tz_vfs,
	  /dev/teei_fp and /dev/teei_config).

	  Its own client API is built in, so the kernel's generic TEE subsystem
	  is not required. This is vendor code carried over from the phone's
	  GPL kernel: it is not upstreamable and only builds against the
	  Microtrust secure OS of the matching board.

	  Say M to build it as the module microtrust_teei. The device tree node
	  it binds to (microtrust,utos) is disabled by default: a wrong secure
	  world description freezes the phone at boot.
